 | `rcode/register-hash` | 733 |\n| `add0178e7de1` | `1bf1ac57333e` | `dc/image-hash` | 1641 |\n| `aed64f20d715` | `25d418f9afbb` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 196 |\n| `b3ee9e8c72e8` | `e0e8fdfca9d9` | `:fingerprint` of `db/project-datoms` on `vm/ast->datoms` | 32 |\n| `c0aefe2fa287` | `70de2f461733` | `rcode/register-hash` | 166 |\n| `e00c3b0d6325` | `9ab244f27567` | `dc/image-hash` | 784 |\n| `e780fb5067ce` | `decbf54ad753` | `rcode/register-hash` | 473 |\n| `e971cd9b084c` | `688b2b450aac` | `dc/image-hash` | 691 |\n| `eb70fa6d6b3a` | `f284fcb321a3` | `dc/image-hash` | 497 |\n| `f53e884408c9` | `e2fac210d293` | `rcode/register-hash` | 355 |\n| `f74e6e75631b` | `c4413a954f8a` | `dc/image-hash` | 594 |\n| `f86f480ae243` | `3c0622436b68` | `rcode/register-hash` | 56 |\n| `fb7626101d5e` | `236b6decefd5` | `rcode/register-hash` | 797 |\n| `fe79f9ab7e0a` | `f35503a87fbd` | `dc/image-hash` | 745 |\n| `handoff-v2:afe9e3ac1c3c` | `52c7efaa3967` | `jing/segment-key` | 227 |\n| `linker-R:c0aefe2fa287` | `bc06914564a0` | `rcode/register-hash` | 1655 |\n| `py:b9dbaeff80b3` | `577aabfb8632` | `jing/segment-key` | 813 |\n| `pysp:0971cc1ef48a` | `6c39c4b94a08` | `jing/segment-key` | 72 |\n\n## A-address gates\n\n`git diff --quiet` passed for `corpus.cljc` (32 pins), `rows_test.cljc`\n(20 pins), `layout_test.cljc`, the surviving safepoint harness, and the\n`rows-checkpoint-v3.txt` / `ledger-v2.txt` fixtures. They are byte-for-byte\nunchanged from HEAD. The broad VM suite exercises the corpus, rows, layout\nand harness gates. Python's prelude-independent program root is unchanged.\nNo A address or root pin was regenerated.\n\n## Verification\n\nAll final runs exited 0. Tests ran in foreground JVM processes; no commit,\nNode lane or Dart lane was run, as required by this brief. Logs are under\n`target/8ab/`.\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `clj -M:kondo --lint <changed Clojure files>` plus the whole `dao.jing` source/test family | 0 errors, 0 warnings |\n| Focused quick, `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n <each touched test namespace>` | 250 tests, 8,483 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| Focused slow, `clojure -M:test -i :slow -n <each touched test namespace>` | 17 tests, 200 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| Broad VM, command below | 1,149 tests, 25,237 assertions, 0 failures/errors |\n| `clojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'dao\\.jing.*'` | 233 tests, 10,383 assertions, 0 failures/errors; this family has no tagged slow tests |\n| Descriptor comparison against original HEAD forms | Exact two-row change for both descriptors; versions 2/4 unchanged |\n| Two final reproduction runs and `cmp` | Byte-identical output; exact handoff fixture bytes also verified |\n| `git diff --check` | Clean |\n\nBroad VM command:\n\n```sh\nclojure -M:test -e :slow -r 'yin\\.vm\\.(debruijn|semantic-register|linker|ucf)\\..*' -n yin.vm.pipeline-test\n```\n\nFocused namespaces: `yin.vm.debruijn-test`, `yin.vm.debruijn-code-test`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn-register-code-test`, `yin.vm.debruijn-register-compile-test`,\n`yin.vm.debruijn.stack-parity-test`, `yin.vm.linker-test`,\n`yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test`,\n`yang.python.antlr.linked-prelude-test`, and\n`yang.python.antlr.linked-safepoint-test`. The final quick run additionally\nincludes `yin.vm.ucf.handoff-v2-census-test` for the changed fixture.\nThe C4 slow oracle completed 10 root programs and 8 module bodies across\nboth old/new backend families.\n\nThe first broad run could not load the absent generated Python parser.\n`clojure -M:antlr-gen` generated it after downloading the two checksum-pinned\nJava support files with network access. Sandboxed Jing/VM runs also failed\nthe real loopback socket tests; rerunning with approved local socket access\npassed. These environment failures were resolved without source changes.\nThe first broad run additionally exposed the stale handoff fixture, which\nwas regenerated before the final passing run.\n\n## Mutants\n\nEach mutant was applied alone after `cp` backup. Its diff was saved,\nits JVM test command exited 1 with the failures below, and the backup was\nrestored with `cp`. Restoration passed `git diff --no-index --quiet` against\nthe backup, and the before/after `git diff -- <file>` outputs were identical.\nThe real index was untouched. The final quick/broad suites passed after all\nfour restorations.\n\n| Mutant | Catching assertion / suite | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| H `image-hash` left on `jing/sha256` | `debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 4 failures, 0 errors |\n| Register descriptor `:hash` row left `:sha256` | `debruijn-register-code-test/golden-descriptor-hash-test` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n| `:const-long` H pin regenerated using SHA-256 over the **current** descriptor hash and image encoding | `debruijn-code-test/golden-corpus-bytes-and-hash` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n| Old worked-example H `52791d4a…` retained in the new lowerer's golden | `semantic-register.derive-test/stack-goldens` | 1 failure, 0 errors |\n\nAll four mutants were caught. Wrong-algorithm mutant value was computed with\n`(jing/sha256 (str dc/descriptor-hash (dc/encode-image [[:const 42] [:return]])))`,\nthen placed in the pin; it was not invented.\n\n\n## Deviations and design findings\n\n- The plan says 11 pins in `derive_test`; the code has 10 H plus 10 R pins.\n  All 20 were regenerated. `debruijn_code_test` has four additional H\n  goldens omitted from the inventory; all four were regenerated. Stack\n  parity has four distinct image/H rows and four wire-byte pins, rather\n  than the plan's six hashes/two hex images. Every wire-byte pin stayed.\n- The old register compiler test still exists until 8e. It has 11 image\n  checksum pins, not 12. Removing only its duplicated descriptor golden\n  while leaving stale checksum pins makes this slice fail. Those 11 pins\n  were regenerated from their printed images, preserving all image and\n  execution assertions until the planned deletion. No shim was added.\n- Production's named-root pairing verifier still uses the old register\n  allocator until 8c. Its authentic-pairing test explicitly produces the\n  old allocation locally; general linker helpers use `derive` as requested.\n  Switching production here would silently import an 8c semantic change.\n- `py` and `pysp` manifest addresses already change in 8ab because their\n  derivation outputs and checksum-keyed indexes embed H/R. Both were\n  regenerated now, with printed complete manifest maps. Their contract/map\n  shape and production pipeline remain current; 8c necessarily regenerates\n  these manifests again when that pipeline and manifest shape change. The\n  plan's claim that manifests move only once in the whole phase does not\n  match this intermediate slice dependency.\n- The registry/classification documents had stale claims that the register\n  implementation was absent and that four SHA-256 sites were current.\n  They now describe the six implemented BLAKE3 sites. Historical H0/H1\n  no-change obligations remain historical; SHA-256 remains an explicit,\n  permanent Jing registry member and the DHT routing contract stays SHA-256.\n- The broad suite found `handoff-v2.txt` embeds an H checksum in its CBOR\n  payload, despite the plan's claim that old transport fixtures contain no\n  H/R. Its plain hex does not expose the ASCII digest to a raw hash grep.\n  The fixture's image H and checkpoint address were regenerated using the\n  printed image and decoded body. The decoded body differs only by replacing\n  the embedded H throughout; its version, code rows, floats and cursor IDs remain identical; layout\n  structure is unchanged and its H references regenerate with that checksum. The reproduction script also verifies exact\n  fixture bytes. The fixture stays until its planned 8d deletion.\n- A raw root preimage containing old child hashes cannot be regenerated by\n  merely substituting the dimension hash. The essay root was recomputed\n  from its printed AST with the public projection function instead.\n\nNo new architectural defect was found. The pairing/manifest sequencing\nissues above are existing phase-plan boundaries and are kept explicit.\n\n## Files and line counts\n\nTracked-file counts are added/deleted lines from `git diff --numstat`.\n\n| File | Added | Deleted |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| `docs/design/dao.jing.call-site-classification.md` | 19 | 22 |\n| `docs/design/dao.jing.hash-registry.md` | 25 | 39 |\n| `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.derivations.md` | 1 | 1 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc` | 5 | 5 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc` | 11 | 17 |\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc` | 11 | 10 |\n| `test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/handoff-v2.txt` | 18 | 18 |\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_prelude_test.cljc` | 3 | 3 |\n| `test/yang/python/antlr/linked_safepoint_test.cljc` | 3 | 3 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn/stack_parity_test.cljc` | 11 | 10 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc` | 5 | 13 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code_test.cljc` | 1 | 1 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_register_compile_test.cljc` | 12 | 20 |\n| `test/yin/vm/debruijn_test.cljc` | 8 | 8 |\n| `test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc` | 15 | 13 |\n| `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/derive_test.cljc` | 11 | 11 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-8ab-regen.clj` (new) | 41 | 0 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-8ab-intermediates.edn` (new) | 1670 | 0 |\n| `collab/1792620000000-engineer-8ab.report.md` (new) | 251 | 0 |\n\n19 files changed: 16 tracked files and 3 new artifacts (this report, the\nreproduction script and the printed-intermediate EDN file). Pre-existing\nuntracked prompt, plan and agent stdout files were left alone.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
